list_entities — flagged tool mirror (NOT scheduled)
====================================================

status: flagged (2026-07-12), not planned for implementation.
spec: "resource-read tool mirrors" under "mcp resources".

what it is: a builtin tool alias for the
isabelle://theory/{name}/entities resource, same motivation and same
non-implementation rationale as plans/read_theory (uneven client
resource support; mirrors duplicate the surface). trigger to
revisit: an evals/ failure where an agent cannot reach entities
through resources/read.

advertised metadata (sketch)
----------------------------

name          list_entities
description   "List the entities a theory defines — consts, types,
              classes, facts, locales — with kinds and positions.
              Image theories answer from name-space entries, loaded
              theories from live snapshot markup; filesystem-tier
              theories answer with their tier (\"not checked —
              load_theory to get semantics\"). `kind` and `prefix`
              filter. Same content as the
              isabelle://theory/{name}/entities resource."
inputSchema   {"type": "object",
               "properties": {
                 "theory": {"type": "string"},
                 "kind": {"type": "string",
                          "enum": ["const", "type", "class", "fact",
                                   "locale"]},
                 "prefix": {"type": "string"}},
               "required": ["theory"]}
annotations   {"readOnlyHint": true, "idempotentHint": true,
               "openWorldHint": false}

backing: zero new mechanism — the handler calls the same
theory_entities path (mcp_session.scala) the resource uses:
image_theory normalization, image tier via the MCP.ir "entities"
fname (Name_Space filtering in MCP_Repl.thy), loaded tier via
entity-def markup on the snapshot, ?kind=&prefix= filtering. same
sharing rule as read_theory: one function, two surfaces.

tests (sketch): [scala unit] row + dispatch + parity with the
resource read; [e2e] entities of an image theory by tool and by
resource, identical payloads.
